 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "my oven fan keeps going after ive turned the oven off, been about 20 mins now. is it broken??"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "It is not necessarily broken, as most modern ovens have a cooling fan that runs automatically to cool the appliance down after use. This behavior is normal and should stop once the internal temperature has dropped sufficiently. This sounds like normal behaviour rather than a fault: Cooling fans keep running after an oven (or a combination microwave) is switched off until the inside has cooled, often 10-30 minutes. It would be worth a closer look if the fan never stops even when the oven is cold. Next: Work out which fan: cavity fan (uneven cooking) vs cooling fan (quiet whirring, controls getting hot). Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its a quiet steady whirr and warm air is coming out of the slot above the door. no grinding. it does stop on its own eventually, usually after 20-30 mins. so is that the cooling fan then?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, that is the oven’s cooling fan. It runs to cool down internal components and typically continues for a short time after use before stopping automatically. Next: If the controls/fascia are getting hot, stop using the oven until the cooling fan is repaired. Let me know what you find."
  }
 ],
